From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] HTMLViewer: the open source licences do not cost the reader their files

设置 > 关于平板电脑 > 法律信息 > 第三方许可 opens this viewer, and on V85 the
first thing it does is ask 「要允许 HTML 查看程序访问您设备上的照片、媒体内容和
文件吗？」 on a black title bar. Refusing closes the page, so the only way to
read the licences of an open source system is to hand a viewer the reader's
own files.

It asks because `requestPermissionAndLoad()` treats every `file:` URI as a
file on shared storage. Settings hands it `file:///system/etc/NOTICE.html.gz`
(`SettingsLicenseActivity.showSelectedFile` -> `Uri.fromFile`), a file on the
read-only system image that every app may read and that
READ_EXTERNAL_STORAGE has nothing to do with: that permission governs the
shared volumes under /storage. The check now asks that question --
`StorageManager.getStorageVolume()` returns the shared volume a file is on,
and null for one that is on none -- so a licence opens straight away and a
file the reader really did put on the shared volume still asks, as before.

The activity's theme was `Theme.DeviceDefault`, the dark one, which is where
the black title bar comes from. Every other screen in this system is white
with black text (rule 1 of docs/design/eink-ui.md), and a full-width black
bar appearing and going is the shape rule 9 keeps off this panel, so it
becomes `Theme.DeviceDefault.Light` like the rest.

